# Security

Authorize every protected operation on the server. A hidden link or a client-side role check is not access control.

## Rules

- Verify identity, role, organization membership, and resource access on the server.
- Enforce tenant isolation. One client organization must not read another organization's data.
- Plan for PostgreSQL Row Level Security on tenant and personal data.
- Never send secret keys, privileged credentials, or the Supabase service-role key to the browser.
- Validate all external input on the server.
- Use transactions when related writes must succeed or fail together.
- Make financial operations and inbound webhooks idempotent. Verify webhook signatures.
- Do not store card numbers or sensitive banking credentials.
- Do not mark work paid because an invoice was created. Keep work approval, earnings calculation, earnings approval, payout initiation, and payout confirmation separate.
- Do not send private customer data to an external AI provider without authorization and a configured data-handling policy.
- Do not invent certifications, customer proof, or legal claims.

```typescript
// Bad: the browser decides and the service role key is exposed
const supabase = createClient(url, process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY);

// Good: a server-only client uses the privileged key, after an authorization check
const supabase = createServerClient(); // server module, key is not NEXT_PUBLIC_
await assertCanReadProject(session, projectId);
```
